{"case_id": "p03", "rep": 0, "suite": "practice", "variant": "moonshotai__kimi-k3@low", "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k3", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Algebraic Expressions", "remediate"], "output": "QUESTION: Hiya! 👋 Let's warm up with this one: Simplify the expression by adding the like terms: 3x + 5x − 2x + 4. Show me your steps — you can do this!\nFINAL_ANSWER: 6x + 4", "pred": null, "grade": {"parsed": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 2.719, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 719, "output_tokens": 87, "reasoning_tokens": 15, "cost_usd": 0.001491, "served_models": ["moonshotai/kimi-k3"], "hosts": ["Makora"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:41:02"}
{"case_id": "p02", "rep": 0, "suite": "practice", "variant": "moonshotai__kimi-k3@low", "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k3", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Algebraic Equations", "challenge"], "output": "QUESTION: Hey! Let's stretch those algebra muscles today 💪 Solve for x: 3(2x − 4) = 2x + 8. Remember to multiply out the brackets first, then collect the x-terms on one side. Show me each step!\nFINAL_ANSWER: x = 5", "pred": null, "grade": {"parsed": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.703, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 1053, "output_tokens": 127, "reasoning_tokens": 50, "cost_usd": 0.001065, "served_models": ["moonshotai/kimi-k3"], "hosts": ["Sail Research"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:41:03"}
{"case_id": "p21", "rep": 0, "suite": "practice", "variant": "moonshotai__kimi-k3@low", "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k3", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Patterns, sequences and series", "practice", "grade12"], "output": "QUESTION: Hi! 👋 Let's practise arithmetic sequences. Consider the sequence: 7; 11; 15; 19; ... (a) Write down the common difference. (b) Determine the 20th term of the sequence. (c) Hence, calculate the sum of the first 20 terms. Show all your working!\nFINAL_ANSWER: d = 4; T₂₀ = 83; S₂₀ = 900", "pred": null, "grade": {"parsed": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 2.609, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 884, "output_tokens": 238, "reasoning_tokens": 133, "cost_usd": 0.003739, "served_models": ["moonshotai/kimi-k3"], "hosts": ["Wafer"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:41:04"}
{"case_id": "p23", "rep": 0, "suite": "practice", "variant": "moonshotai__kimi-k3@low", "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k3", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Exponential and logarithmic functions", "remediate", "grade12"], "output": "QUESTION: Hi there! 💪 Let's warm up with an exponential equation. Solve for x: 3^(x+2) = 27. Hint: try writing 27 as a power of 3, then compare the exponents. Show me your steps!\nFINAL_ANSWER: x = 1", "pred": null, "grade": {"parsed": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 2.42, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 860, "output_tokens": 178, "reasoning_tokens": 103, "cost_usd": 0.001946, "served_models": ["moonshotai/kimi-k3"], "hosts": ["Wafer"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:41:06"}
{"case_id": "p22", "rep": 0, "suite": "practice", "variant": "moonshotai__kimi-k3@low", "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k3", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Finance, growth and decay", "challenge", "grade12"], "output": "QUESTION: Hey! 💪 Here's a challenge: Thabo invests R80 000 at 9% p.a. compounded monthly. After 2 years the rate changes to 10% p.a. compounded annually. Calculate the value of the investment at the end of 5 years in total. Show each stage of your working!\nFINAL_ANSWER: R127 394,30 (approximately R127 394)", "pred": null, "grade": {"parsed": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 4.753, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 882, "output_tokens": 804, "reasoning_tokens": 707, "cost_usd": 0.007952, "served_models": ["moonshotai/kimi-k3"], "hosts": ["Wafer"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:41:07"}
{"case_id": "p24", "rep": 0, "suite": "practice", "variant": "moonshotai__kimi-k3@low", "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k3", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Functions and inverse functions", "practice", "grade12"], "output": "QUESTION: Hi! 🌟 Here's a good one: Given f(x) = 2x + 6. (a) Write down the equation of the inverse of f in the form f⁻¹(x) = ... (b) Hence calculate the value of f⁻¹(10). Show your working step by step, and remember — to find the inverse, swap x and y, then make y the subject!\nFINAL_ANSWER: f⁻¹(x) = (x − 6)/2; f⁻¹(10) = 2", "pred": null, "grade": {"parsed": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 4.537, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 829, "output_tokens": 203, "reasoning_tokens": 77, "cost_usd": 0.002168, "served_models": ["moonshotai/kimi-k3"], "hosts": ["Wafer"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:41:08"}
{"case_id": "p25", "rep": 0, "suite": "practice", "variant": "moonshotai__kimi-k3@low", "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k3", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Trigonometry - compound angles", "challenge", "grade12"], "output": "QUESTION: Hey! 💪 Here's a challenge: Given that sin A = 3/5 with A in the second quadrant, and cos B = -5/13 with B in the third quadrant, determine the exact value of sin(A + B) *without* using a calculator. Show all your steps — first find cos A and sin B, then use the compound angle identity!\nFINAL_ANSWER: sin(A + B) = 33/65", "pred": null, "grade": {"parsed": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.311, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 1149, "output_tokens": 208, "reasoning_tokens": 103, "cost_usd": 0.003046, "served_models": ["moonshotai/kimi-k3"], "hosts": ["InferenceNet"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:41:09"}
{"case_id": "p05", "rep": 0, "suite": "practice", "variant": "moonshotai__kimi-k3@low", "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k3", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Exponents", "practice"], "output": "QUESTION: Hey! 👋 Let's practise exponents today. Use the exponent laws to simplify this one: 3x² × 4x⁵. Write your answer in its simplest form, and show me your steps — what's the coefficient, and what happens to the exponents?\nFINAL_ANSWER: 12x⁷", "pred": null, "grade": {"parsed": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 12.554, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 992, "output_tokens": 126, "reasoning_tokens": 46, "cost_usd": 0.001474, "served_models": ["moonshotai/kimi-k3"], "hosts": ["Wafer"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:41:13"}
{"case_id": "p06", "rep": 0, "suite": "practice", "variant": "moonshotai__kimi-k3@low", "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k3", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Integers", "remediate"], "output": "QUESTION: Hi! Let's warm up with some integers 💪 Calculate the following, showing each step: a) −7 + 4 b) −3 − (−6) c) −5 × (−2) Take your time and remember: two negatives together make a positive!\nFINAL_ANSWER: a) −3, b) 3, c) 10", "pred": null, "grade": {"parsed": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 1.928, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 761, "output_tokens": 167, "reasoning_tokens": 78, "cost_usd": 0.001804, "served_models": ["moonshotai/kimi-k3"], "hosts": ["Wafer"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:17:35"}
{"case_id": "p08", "rep": 0, "suite": "practice", "variant": "moonshotai__kimi-k3@low", "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k3", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers", "practice"], "output": "QUESTION: Hi! 😊 Let's practise whole numbers. Write 360 as a product of its prime factors, using exponents. Show each step of your working — a factor tree works great. Then tell me your final answer in exponent form.\nFINAL_ANSWER: 2³ × 3² × 5", "pred": null, "grade": {"parsed": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 4.132, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 955, "output_tokens": 95, "reasoning_tokens": 19, "cost_usd": 0.001713, "served_models": ["moonshotai/kimi-k3"], "hosts": ["Makora"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:17:37"}
